Z||000000||Roy||05-18-99||07:55 PM||||I was thinking of mounting a nos tank there. But I was a little concerned if the car was rear ended. Isnt there a good chance, if the tank was puncture by the collision, it could explode? 
Z||000001||theogre||05-18-99||08:07 PM||||actually it's more likely that the tank will get shoved thru something. the tank is far stranger than the surounding materials.<p>You may have problems draining the bottle completely. the pickup tube needs to go in a certain position, and preferably valve toward the front. That oreintation may only be posible up front. there is enough room over the spare if you make a bracket. tho you won't have room for it and a sunroof if your car has that.
Z||000002||Shaun41178||05-18-99||09:37 PM||||I have my nos bottle mounted in the trunk<p>I too have concerns about the car being rearended and imploding the bottle.  Afterall the contents are under about 2k psi or more.  I can't remember the exact number off hand but it is very high<p>I would like to move it to the front.  I have  sort of designed a way to mount the bottle in the front and keep the spare tire in there too although I have thought about just keeping some fix-a-flat and take the spare out completely.  I am very lazy and have yet to tackle this project as it will result in the rerouting of the nitrous plumbing.<p>With my bottle mounted in the trunk there is more then enough room for it to be mounted in the proper position.  it is recommended that the valve and such be facing a certain direction and there is plenty of space for it to be mounted properly in the trunk.<p>If anyone would like to see pics of my nitrous setup you can see them at my homepage at  http://members.aol.com/shaun41178<p>
